{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"copying","title":"Immutability & Copying","group":"Arrays & Objects","order":29,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Assignment copies references. To copy data you choose between a shallow copy (top level only) and a deep copy (everything) — and immutable updates build new objects instead of mutating old ones.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-stack-2\"></i>Shallow copies share nested objects</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const original = { name: \"Asha\", skills: [\"js\"], meta: { level: 1 } };\nconst shallow = { ...original };\nshallow.name = \"Ravi\";          // top level: independent\nshallow.skills.push(\"css\");     // nested: SHARED\nshallow.meta.level = 99;\nconsole.log(original);\nconsole.log(shallow.skills === original.skills);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ name: 'Asha', skills: [ 'js', 'css' ], meta: { level: 99 } }\ntrue</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Shallow copy tools</th><th>Arrays</th><th>Objects</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spread</td><td><code>[...arr]</code></td><td><code>{...obj}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Built-ins</td><td><code>arr.slice()</code>, <code>Array.from(arr)</code>, <code>arr.concat()</code></td><td><code>Object.assign({}, obj)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-copy-check\"></i>Deep copy with structuredClone</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const original = {\n  when: new Date(0),\n  tags: new Set([\"a\"]),\n  lookup: new Map([[\"k\", { deep: true }]]),\n  nested: { list: [1, [2, 3]] },\n};\noriginal.self = original;              // cycles are fine\nconst clone = structuredClone(original);\nclone.nested.list[1].push(4);\nconsole.log(original.nested.list, clone.nested.list);\nconsole.log(clone.when instanceof Date, clone.tags, clone.self === clone);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 1, [ 2, 3 ] ] [ 1, [ 2, 3, 4 ] ]\ntrue Set(1) { 'a' } true</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Point { constructor(x) { this.x = x; } norm() { return Math.abs(this.x); } }\nconst copy = structuredClone(new Point(-3));\nconsole.log(copy, copy instanceof Point);\ntry {\n  structuredClone({ fn() {} });\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.name);\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ x: -3 } false\nDataCloneError</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Dates / Map / Set</th><th>Cycles</th><th>Functions</th><th>Class instances</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spread / <code>assign</code></td><td>shared refs (shallow)</td><td>shared</td><td>copied (ref)</td><td>prototype lost for spread</td></tr><tr><td><code>JSON.parse(JSON.stringify())</code></td><td>Date → string, Map/Set → <code>{}</code></td><td>throws</td><td>dropped</td><td>plain object</td></tr><tr><td><code>structuredClone</code></td><td>✔ preserved</td><td>✔</td><td>throws <code>DataCloneError</code></td><td>plain object (prototype lost)</td></tr><tr><td>Custom recursive / lodash <code>cloneDeep</code></td><td>✔</td><td>✔ (with a map)</td><td>kept by reference</td><td>configurable</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-refresh\"></i>Immutable update patterns</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const state = { user: { name: \"Asha\", prefs: { theme: \"light\" } }, todos: [{ id: 1, done: false }] };\n\nconst next = {\n  ...state,\n  user: { ...state.user, prefs: { ...state.user.prefs, theme: \"dark\" } },\n  todos: state.todos.map((t) =&gt; (t.id === 1 ? { ...t, done: true } : t)),\n};\nconsole.log(state.user.prefs.theme, next.user.prefs.theme);\nconsole.log(state.todos[0].done, next.todos[0].done);\nconsole.log(state.user === next.user, state === next);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>light dark\nfalse true\nfalse false</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Why it matters</div><p>Immutable updates copy only the <em>path</em> that changed and share the rest (structural sharing). That lets React, Redux and memoisation detect changes with a cheap <code>===</code>.</p></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Instead of (mutating)</th><th>Write (immutable)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>arr.push(x)</code></td><td><code>[...arr, x]</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>arr.splice(i, 1)</code></td><td><code>arr.filter((_, j) =&gt; j !== i)</code> or <code>arr.toSpliced(i, 1)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>arr[i] = v</code></td><td><code>arr.with(i, v)</code> or <code>arr.map(...)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>arr.sort()</code></td><td><code>arr.toSorted()</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>obj.k = v</code></td><td><code>{ ...obj, k: v }</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>delete obj.k</code></td><td><code>const { k, ...rest } = obj</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Shallow copy vs deep copy?</summary><div><p>A shallow copy duplicates only the top level; nested objects are still shared with the original. A deep copy recursively duplicates everything, so the copies are fully independent. Use spread for shallow, <code>structuredClone</code> for deep.</p></div></details></section>"}